From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:35:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: a torch failure should grey the tile out, not kill
 the shell

FlashlightControllerImpl catches CameraAccessException around
CameraManager.setTorchMode() and nothing else. But setTorchMode() converts a service-side
refusal into an unchecked IllegalArgumentException, and the call runs on a background
executor, so any such refusal is a fatal uncaught exception on that thread:

    FATAL EXCEPTION: SysUiBg
    java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: setTorchMode:2394: Camera "0" has no flashlight
        at FlashlightControllerImpl$$ExternalSyntheticLambda0.run

Tapping the tile then restarts SystemUI. Reached here on a device whose camera HAL reports a
flash unit in its static metadata -- dumpsys media.camera says "Has a flash unit: true" -- but
whose HAL returns an error when actually asked to light it; cameraserver maps that to -ENOSYS
and prints the misleading "has no flashlight".

Catch RuntimeException as well and report it the same way as an access error. A HAL that
declines to light the torch is a device-support problem, and the tile already has a path for
that: dispatchError() greys it out.
---
 .../statusbar/policy/FlashlightControllerImpl.java        | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/policy/FlashlightControllerImpl.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/policy/FlashlightControllerImpl.java
index 5dcafb37f57e..c00658d27ddd 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/policy/FlashlightControllerImpl.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/policy/FlashlightControllerImpl.java
@@ -135,6 +135,14 @@ public class FlashlightControllerImpl implements FlashlightController {
                     } catch (CameraAccessException e) {
                         Log.e(TAG, "Couldn't set torch mode", e);
                         dispatchError();
+                    } catch (RuntimeException e) {
+                        // setTorchMode() turns a service-side refusal into an unchecked
+                        // IllegalArgumentException, and this runs on a background executor, so
+                        // anything not caught here takes SystemUI down with it. A HAL that
+                        // declines to light the torch is a device-support problem; it should
+                        // grey the tile out, not restart the shell.
+                        Log.e(TAG, "Couldn't set torch mode", e);
+                        dispatchError();
                     }
                 }
             }
